            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 5,
            "text": "Thank you, Kevin, for the \"how\".\nI've committed the changes now in svn rev 90838  - to be backported to the R-4-6 branch.\nNote that I've *not* used `identical()` but a version of `all.equal()`, as indeed\nit was found that in another such case (\"Ra\" vs \"Rao\" method) \n`identical()` would have been logically correct,\nbut unfortunately modern computer runtime / parallelization / ???\nleads to not-to-the-bit-reproducible behaviour, and a version of `all.equal()` was needed even in such a case.",
